er beneficiaries of a pension trust have a property interest in the trust\'s assets and can sue when those assets are lost due to disloyal or imprudent actions by the trustees.\n  - id: 22-704, name: Vidal, Under Sec. of Comm. v. Elster, description: The case concerns the constitutionality of a federal law restricting trademark registration for marks referring to living individuals without their consent, with the Petitioner arguing it is viewpoint neutral and does not restrict speech.\n  - id: 22-148, name: Jack Daniel\'s Properties, Inc. v. VIP Products, description: This case is about a dog toy company that used Jack Daniel\'s trademark and trade dress to associate its whiskey with dog poop, leading to a dispute over trademark infringement and dilution.\n  - id: 23-50, name: Chiaverini v. City of Napoleon, description: This case, Chiaverini v. City of Napoleon, involves a dispute over the requirements for a malicious prosecution claim under the Fourth Amendment, specifically whether a plaintiff must show that a seizure was caused by the malicious prosecution rather than another factor.\n  - id: 22-1078, name: Warner Chappell Music, Inc. v. Nealy, description: This case is about whether a copyright plaintiff can recover damages for acts that occurred more than three years before filing suit, and whether the discovery rule applies to extend this period.\n  - id: 18-1447, name: Republic of Hungary v. Simon, description: The case concerns whether a US court can hear claims against Hungary for property confiscations during World War II, despite the US having previously settled its own claims with Hungary and the potential for international friction.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this form